Engine: cloud-crawler-core. It is written in saulpatinojr/HCW-CloudCrawler_App and adopted here unchanged
(docs/adr/0001-lab-edition-never-calls-azure.md). This edition installs that repository's release wheel as a
dependency, pinned by URL in pyproject.toml (the `# CORE_REF` line) and by sha256 in uv.lock; core-update.yml opens the
pull request that moves the pin. The engine's package metadata declares MIT, the same licence as this repository; no
engine source is kept here.
  Source: https://github.com/saulpatinojr/HCW-CloudCrawler_App (packages/cloud-crawler-core).

Lab image: the image built from infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile and published by publish-images.yml as
docker.io/hybridcloudworks/img-cc-lab-addon installs that wheel from uv.lock, and its label
org.opencontainers.image.licenses says "MIT". The base image, Python and the other installed packages keep their own
licences.

Azure MCP Server: this edition neither includes nor runs Microsoft's Azure MCP Server. It never fetches evidence; it
reads only what is uploaded or what the website hands in, which may be results the website obtained from that server.

The pane's theme tokens (web/theme.css) are copied from the hybridcloudworks.com website repository
(HCW-HybridCloudWorks, frontend/src/index.css) on 2026-10-10. The pane loads no fonts from the site.

Samples and test data are fictional: subscription 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 and hcw-sample-* names (the
storage accounts, whose names Azure forbids a hyphen in, are hcwsamplest*). Nothing in samples/ is or ever was a real
estate.

